From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rakina Zata Amni <rakina@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 04:05:08 -0700
Subject: Stop notifying observers if NavigationRequest is deleted

On Android, a WebContentsObserver can synchronously delete the
NavigationRequest from DidStartNavigation(), DidRedirectNavigation()
or ReadyToCommitNavigation(), e.g. when a WebView app calls
stopLoading() from its navigation callback. https://crrev.com/c/7781148
made NavigationRequest handle this, but WebContentsImpl still notified
the remaining observers with the deleted NavigationHandle.

Add NotifyObserversUntilNavigationDeleted(), which stops notifying
observers once the NavigationRequest is deleted, and use it for those
notifications. The remaining observers still get DidFinishNavigation(),
which is called when the NavigationRequest is deleted.

